Description: This workshop aims to introduce two Bioconductor packages,
 scider and hoodscanR, specialised for complementary downstream analyses on
 spatial transcriptomics data. Participants will learn neighbourhood-level
 analysis (probabilities, entropy/perplexity, clustering, and co-localisation)
 with hoodscanR, and density modelling, ROI/contour detection, and
 density-driven analyses with scider, using a Xenium breast cancer dataset.
Maintainer: Ning Liu <ning.liu@adelaide.edu.au>
